WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
In 1861, de Fabeck painted Dhaka from the Buriganga.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:14.000
Look at the water first. The boats sit low; the city rises behind them.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:21.000
In 1952, Clarence Sorensen photographed the city from the river.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:28.000
In the photograph, the far bank is a thin line between water and sky.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:35.000
At Sadarghat in 2007, passengers passed between the wharf and the launches.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:42.000
Three views across 146 years. In each one, the river is a way into Dhaka.
